{"id":"1y0uft4","permalink":"https://www.reddit.com/r/aigamedev/comments/1y0uft4/","title":"Check out my 0 asset procedurally generated cat wizard game","author":"will-QA-for-food","created_utc":1795149629,"created":"2026-11-20","score":16,"num_comments":4,"flair":"Commercial Self Promotion","status":"pending","media":{"kind":"reddit_video","url":"https://v.redd.it/pe1y4hl14p2i1","still":"media/1y0uft4.jpg","video":{"hls":"https://v.redd.it/pe1y4hl14p2i1/HLSPlaylist.m3u8?f=hd%2CsubsAll%2ChlsSpecOrder%2Cvp9&v=1&a=1797741644%2CYjhkMWY2ZTVlNWI0NmY2YTQwM2NhNDI4OTQ0ZWNiMTI2YTQxZTNhNGQyZTA5OTZmZTgyZTIwNzkzNDg3NDM4OQ%3D%3D","mp4":"https://v.redd.it/pe1y4hl14p2i1/CMAF_1080.mp4?source=fallback"},"thumbnail":"https://external-preview.redd.it/dGltd3Q4bTE0cDJpMcpBk5YfGcH8u2mPmh_W8Prle-UtfzweQN9tT04k_s0p.png?width=140&height=78&format=jpg&auto=webp&s=1fa6f5fd49409d0130b5d859296143eb874297fc"},"selftext":"All assets are generated at runtime (Sounds/Graphics). It's called \"Nine Lives Below\" I was trying to capture the aspects of Noita that I really enjoyed and balanced out my features for a 4-player co-op experience.\n\n  \nWhat drove this forward was having AI understand that no assets could be leveraged in the creation, and I think it turned out pretty ok.","url":"https://v.redd.it/pe1y4hl14p2i1","signals":{"body_len":351,"author_followup_chars":551,"author_followup_count":2,"score":16,"num_comments":5,"kind":"reddit_video","flair":"Commercial Self Promotion"},"comments":[{"id":"19swl93ee6qm9","author":"DeanRayGames","body":"Looks really nice, but I don't understand how these \"zero asset\" games work. I mean, you have what really looks like pixel art assets, but you're saying that the game just draws them mathematically live, in-game? I'm dumb when it comes to this stuff. ","score":2,"created_utc":1795150162,"is_op":false,"replies":[{"id":"19swlgeexso5h","author":"will-QA-for-food","body":"No worries, basically you can have pre-rendered things like images or textures that you use as assets in your game. This project deterministically creates the assets through code when you run the application so technically there aren't any assets, the visuals you see exist because of the underlying code. This gives you a couple benefits like low install sizes (this game is <100mb) and you can also run this headless for testing purposes (No actual visuals, just simulation)\n\nHope that helps. 🫠 ","score":2,"created_utc":1795150435,"is_op":true,"replies":[]},{"id":"19swp2it8hxz6","author":"HaMMeReD","body":"I can't speak for op, but the concept of asset in my game is \"binary free\". Technically an asset, but stored as text so a LLM can work with it quickly. I assume something similar here.\n\n    # Woodcutter in a green coat, axe raised, facing east.\n    language metalrain.sprite 1\n    key woodcutter/swing-1\n    revision 1\n    size 64 40\n    legend . clear\n    legend C 177 117 58\n    legend O 156 76 40\n    legend Q 89 133 79\n    legend b 70 58 64\n    legend c 111 72 39\n    legend k 38 32 46\n    legend o 214 118 52\n    legend q 45 91 68\n    legend s 96 104 122\n    legend t 222 171 126\n    legend w 222 226 232\n    row ..............................cccc..............................\n    row ............................cccccccc............................\n    row ...........................cccccccccc........kkk................\n    row ...........................cCCCCCCCCc.......ssssw...............\n    row ..........................cccccccccccc......ssssw...............\n    row ...........................kttttttttk.......ssssw...............\n    row ...........................ktttttkttk.......ssssw...............\n    row ...........................kttttttttk.......ssssw...............\n    row ...........................kbbttttbbk......kkkkk................\n    row ............................kbbbbbbk.......kckk.................\n    row .............................kbbbbk........kck..................\n    row ..............................kkkk........kkck..................\n    row .............................kkkkkk.......kckk..................\n    row ............................kqqqqqqk......kck...................\n    row ...........................kqqQqqQqqk....kkck...................\n    row ..........................kqqqQqqQqqqk...kckk...................\n    row ..........................kQQQQQQQQQQk...kck....................\n    row ..........................kqqqQqqQkkkk..kkck....................\n    row ..........................kqqqQqqQkookk.kckk....................\n    row ..........................kQQQQQQQkkkokkkck.....................\n    row ..........................kqqqQqqQqqkkokkck.....................\n    row ..........................kqqqQkkQqqqkkkckk.....................\n    row ...........................kkkkkkkkkk.kkckk.....................\n    row ............................kssssssk..kkckk.....................\n    row ............................kooooook..kckkk.....................\n    row ............................koooOOok..kck.......................\n    row ............................koooOOok..kck.......................\n    row ............................koOkkoOk..kck.......................\n    row ............................koOkkoOk..kkk.......................\n    row ............................koOkkoOk............................\n    row ............................koOkkoOk............................\n    row ............................koOkkoOk............................\n    row ............................koOkkoOk............................\n    row ............................koOkkoOk............................\n    row ............................koOkkoOk............................\n    row ............................koOkkoOk............................\n    row ............................kbbbkbbbk...........................\n    row ............................kbbbkbbbk...........................\n    row ............................kbbbkbbbk...........................\n    row ............................kkkkkkkkk...........................\n    ","score":1,"created_utc":1795155297,"is_op":false,"replies":[{"id":"19swp6orwannm","author":"will-QA-for-food","body":"Yes! This is how the sprites work when you drill down.","score":1,"created_utc":1795155452,"is_op":true,"replies":[]}]}]},{"id":"19sxdukrzcklf","author":"DerrickBarra","body":"That does sound like a good iteration process. I wonder if lower end AI like Deepseek would be able to create these at a similar quality since they are simpler to work with? Either way it's very cool that it work, and this technique makes perfect sense for web games and even mobile if the live asset creation isn't a heavy lift for potato PCs and phones","score":2,"created_utc":1795188630,"is_op":false,"replies":[]}]}